# playpick cell: mode=raid boss=gift (The Crimson Gift) spec=paladin:protection
# style=idle size=25 difficulty=heroic view=390x844,touch save=fresh
#
# What is new here: no session has ever run mode=raid boss=gift under idle --
# the only two direct mode=raid pulls of this boss on record (2026-09-30-10
# daily and -14 raid, both warrior, both `good`) showed byMechanic never
# naming gift/bond/stain/turning for the tracked body, for two different
# source reasons (src/sim/boss.ts:3706 excludes the tank role outright;
# the dps pull simply was not rng.pick's one-in-~24 holder). Neither of those
# was idle, so this is the first test of hypothesis 1 (doing nothing wins) on
# this specific boss, and specifically on the tank role the source already
# excludes from the titular mechanic by design -- if idle still clears a
# heroic 25-man clean on the one role structurally walled off from its own
# fight's namesake mechanic, that is the sharpest version of "the player's
# presses have no visible consequence" this line has found yet, since even a
# tank's normal job (holding threat, blocking) is not being asked here.
# upkeep.md's played/idle gap table already lists this fight at 0 (99%/99%),
# so the prediction is a clean idle kill; played here anyway, at heroic rather
# than whatever difficulty that table measured, to see if the gap holds there.
#
# Reached the documented way: an invite hash unlocks the tier it names and
# everything below it, since a fresh save only opens Bonegrinder 10N.
open #b=gift&s=25&h=1
tap class:paladin:protection
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
says
shot open

play idle 70
bill
state
says
shot mid1

play idle 70
bill
state
says
shot mid2

play idle 70
bill
state
says
shot end
